%%vskip 1.0cm
%%sep 0.2cm 0.2cm 7cm
%%vskip 0.8cm
%
W: 1. Villagers all, this frosty tide,
W:    Let your doors swing open wide,
W:    Though wind may follow and snow beside, 
W:    Yet draw us in by your fire to bide,
W:    Joy shall be yours in the morning!
W: 
W: 2. Goodman Joseph toiled through the snow,
W:    Saw the star o'er a stable low;
W:    Mary she might not further go.
W:    Welcome thatch, and litter below!
W:    Joy was hers in the morning!
W: 
W: 3. And then they heard the angels tell
W:    Who were the first to cry Nowell?
W:    The animals all, as it befell,
W:    In the stable where they did dwell
W:    Joy shall be theirs,
W:    Joy shall be hers,
W:    Joy shall be yours in the morning!
